# The HTTP cache: hundreds of raw API responses, regenerable in one `python -m wbso.cli scan`.
# The evidence that matters is already inlined in data/candidates.jsonl and in every briefing, each
# with its source URL and observation date.
data/cache/

# A filled-in sender profile carries the owner's real KVK number, address and phone. The template
# (params/sender_profile.example.json) is committed; the real one never is.
params/sender_profile.json

# Request receipts and run reports: point-in-time, regenerable, and they name the companies we
# looked at. DRYRUN_REPORT.md is the curated version and is committed.
#
# The one exception is probe_report.json: it is the evidence for a claim made in prose — that the
# TenderNed API contains no awarded-supplier field, correcting T26 §7 — and a correction whose
# evidence is untracked is a correction nobody can check.
logs/*
!logs/probe_report.json

# The bulk candidate list, including public business email addresses. Regenerable, and a repository
# is the wrong place for a contact list even when every row is public. The ten dry-run briefings in
# briefings/ stay, because the owner has to be able to read them.
data/candidates.jsonl

# pytest scratch
.pytest_cache/
